      "title": "Prospectus Summary",
      "excerpt": "PROSPECTUS SUMMARY 4 THE OFFERING 11 SUMMARY FINANCIAL AND OTHER DATA 14 RISK FACTORS 18 USE OF PROCEEDS 59 CAPITALIZATION 60 DIVIDEND POLICY 62 DILUTION 63 MANAGEMENT\u2019S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS\n OF OPERATION 65 BUSINESS 82 MANAGEMENT 102 CERTAIN RELATIONSHIPS AND RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS 107 SECURITY OWNERSHIP OF CERTAIN BENEFICIAL OWNERS AND\nMANAGEMENT 110 CERTAIN MARSHALL ISLANDS COMPANY CONSIDERATIONS 111 DESCRIPTION OF CAPITAL STOCK 115 DESCRIPTION OF SECURITIES WE ARE OFFERING 124 TAX CONSIDERATIONS 128 UNDERWRITING 140 SERVICE OF PROCESS AND ENFORCEMENT OF CIVIL LIABILITIES 143 LEGAL MATTERS 143 EXPERTS 143 WHERE YOU CAN FIND ADDITIONAL INFORMATION 143 EXPENSES RELATED TO THE OFFERING 144 INDEX TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS F-1 -i- Table of Contents ABOUT THIS PROSPECTUS This prospectus is part of a registration statement on Form F-1 that we filed wit",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of Proceeds We intend to use the net proceeds from the sale of the securities offered by this prospectus for capital expenditures, including for payment towards the $38.7\u00a0million remaining purchase price for the Aframax tanker we acquired in July 2023,\nor acquisitions of additional vessels which we have not yet identified, which may include vessels in seaborne transportation sectors other than the drybulk and tanker sectors in which we currently operate, working capital, or for other general\ncorporate purposes, or a combination thereof. We expect that the net proceeds from the maximum offering amount of the sale of Units in this offering will be approximately $5.1\u00a0million, net of underwriting discounts and commissions and other\nestimated offering expenses. The expected net proceeds of the offering reflected above does not give effect to the exercise of any Class\u00a0B Warrants issued in ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk Factors See \u201cRisk Factors\u201d and the other information included in this prospectus for a discussion of the factors you should consider carefully before deciding to invest in our securities. 12 Table of Contents (1) The number of Common Shares to be outstanding after this offering is based on 8,742,449 Common Shares\noutstanding as of January 1, 2024 and excludes as of such date: \u2022 14,285,714 Common Shares issuable upon conversion of the 600,000 shares of Series A Convertible Preferred Stock\nwhich are convertible into our Common Shares at a conversion price currently equal to $1.05. The conversion price will be further adjusted to the lowest price of issuance of Common Shares by the Company in any registered offering of Common Shares\nafter the original issuance of Series A Convertible Preferred Shares, including this offering. See \u201cDescription of Capital Stock\u2014Series A Convertible Prefe",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION Dilution or accretion is the amount by which the offering price paid by the purchasers of our Units in this offering exceeds or is lower than,\nrespectively, the net tangible book value per Common Share after the offering. Net tangible book value per Common Share represents our total tangible assets less total liabilities divided by the number of Common Shares outstanding. Our pro forma net tangible book value as of September\u00a030, 2023 after giving effect to the issuance of 794,768 restricted shares in\nNovember 2023, was $50.08 million in total and $5.73 per Common Share. Dilution to Existing Shareholders and Accretion to New Investors if the Maximum\nOffering Amount is Sold As adjusted to give effect to the sale by us of 9,090,909 Units, each consisting of one of our Common Shares\nor one pre-funded warrant, one-half of one Class\u00a0B-1 Warrant and one Class B-2 Warrant, offered by th",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dividend Policy",
      "excerpt": "DIVIDEND POLICY We currently intend to retain our future earnings, if any, to fund the development and growth of our business. Our board of directors will,\nhowever, evaluate our dividend policy consistent with our cash flows and liquidity requirements and we may consider paying dividends on our Common Shares depending on future performance of our business and financial condition. Declaration and\npayment of any future dividend is subject to the discretion of our Board of Directors. The timing and amount of dividend payments will be dependent upon our earnings, financial condition, cash requirements and availability, restrictions in our loan\nagreements, or other financing arrangements, the provisions of Marshall Islands law affecting the payment of distributions to stockholders and other factors, and will be subject to the priority of our Series A Convertible Preferred Stock, which, as\ndes",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
